          "id": "GENUS_LEUCOGERANUS",
          "name": "Leucogeranus",
          "rank": "GENUS",
          "description": "The Siberian crane — a critically endangered, pure white crane that breeds in the Arctic tundra of eastern Siberia and winters in a single wetland in China (Poyang Lake). Its haunting, flute-like calls and spectacular migration route made it a cultural icon in Russia and China. The entire eastern population funnels through Poyang Lake, making it extremely vulnerable to habitat change. A separate central population migrating to India has been functionally extinct since 2002.",
          "lineage": "Palearctic Cranes",
          "children": [
